            <ArticleTitle>[Early VATS(Video-Assisted Thoracoscopic Surgery)Was Effective for a Case of Chylothorax after Lung Cancer Excision].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>791-793</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 66-year-old man underwent a right upper lobectomy and lymph node dissection for lung cancer. We confirmed a milky white pleural effusion after diet initiation on the first postoperative day, and a chylothorax was diagnosed. The patient began a f at-restricted diet; however, the pleural effusion did not decrease. Therefore, we performed VATS(video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery)1 week after surgery with good results. Early VATS for a postoperative chylothorax was useful.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
